  "title": "Erdős Problem #1087",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n)$ be minimal such that every set of $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ contains at most $f(n)$ many sets of four points which are 'degenerate' in the sense that some pair are the same distance apart. Estimate $f(n)$ - in particular, is it true that $f(n)\\leq n^{3+o(1)}$?",
